          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be an abstract
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %em distance function
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} nonnegative
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+real+number"} extended
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/binary+function"} binary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\colon X \times X \to [0,\infty]
          %p
            (For most purposes, we may assume that these distance functions are
            = succeed ":" do
              %em pointwise-bounded
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+real"} upper
            real values, although again we may assume them to be pointwise-bounded and pointwise-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+real+number"} located
            for many purposes.)
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a collection of such distance functions.
          %h3#elementary Elementary axioms
          %p
            Consider the following potential properties of
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em> Reflexivity
                \: For every
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,x) = 0
            %li
              %p
                %em Transitivity
                (a version of the
                = succeed "):" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangle+identity"} triangle identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                there exists an
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
                with
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,z) \leq e(x,y) + e(y,z)
              %p
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z \in X
            %li
              %p
                %em> Symmetry
                \: For every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) \leq e(y,x)
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in X
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) = e(y,x)
            %li
              %p
                %em> Nontriviality
                \: There exists a
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) = 0
                for all
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in X
            %li
              %p
                %em> Filtration
                \: For all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d,e \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in G
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) \leq f(x,y)
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e(x,y) \leq f(x,y)
                for all
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi max
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x,y) = \max(d(x,y), e(x,y))
                for all
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in X
            %li
              %p
                %em> Isotony
                \: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                is a distance function with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e(x,y) \leq d(x,y)
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in X
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
          %h3#sophisticated Sophisticated axioms
          %p
            With the aid of
            %span.newWikiWord
              abstract algebra
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/abstract+algebra"} ?
            (but nothing too fancy), we may view these same 6 axioms in another light, as follows.
          %p
            First, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+set"} function set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty]^{X \times X}
            of all distance functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\colon X \times X \to [0,\infty]
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+group"} lattice
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/star-monoid"} monoid
            under these operations:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The order
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ≤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
                is given pointwise:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi e
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇔
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∀
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \leq e \;\iff\; \forall(x,y\colon X),\; d(x,y) \leq e(x,y) .
            %li
              %p
                The corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/join"} join
                operation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∨
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee
                is also pointwise:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi max
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d \vee e)(x,y) \coloneqq \max(d(x,y), e(x,y)) .
            %li
              %p
                The corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom+element"} bottom element
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero+function"} zero function
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mn 0
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0(x,y) \coloneqq 0 .
            %li
              %p
                The monoid operation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ∘
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \circ
                is defined so:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %munder
                        %mi inf
                        %mrow
                          %mi y
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo +
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi z
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d \circ e)(x,z) \coloneqq \inf_{y \in X} (d(x,y) + e(y,z)) .
            %li
              %p
                The corresponding
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+element"} identity element
                is the infinite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kronecker+delta"} Kronecker delta
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mrow
                        %mo {
                        %mrow
                          %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn 0
                              %mtd
                                %mi if
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi x
                                %mo =
                                %mi y
                                %mo ,
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mn ∞
                              %mtd
                                %mi if
                                %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                %mi x
                                %mo ≠
                                %mi y
                                %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\delta(x,y) \coloneqq \begin{cases}
                      0      &amp; if\; x = y,\\
                      \\infty &amp; if\; x \ne y.
                      \\end{cases}
              %p
                (This works in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
                because we are using extended
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+real+number"} upper
                reals;
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi δ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta(x,y)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infimum"} infimum
                of the set
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi t
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi t
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ∧
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ t\colon \mathbb{R} \;|\; t = 0 \;\wedge\; x = y \}
            %li
              %p
                The
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ↦
                      %msup
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \mapsto d^{\op}
                is defined so:
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi d
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo ,
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^{\op}(x,y) \coloneqq d(y,x) .
          %p Then the same 6 axioms may be expressed as follows:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Reflexivity: For every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi δ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \leq \delta
            %li
              %p
                Transitivity: For every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \leq e \circ e
            %li
              %p
                Symmetry: For every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ≤
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \leq e^{\op}
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = e^op
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi d
                          %mi op
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d^op \in G
            %li
              %p
                Nontriviality: There exists a
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 0
            %li
              %p
                Filtration: For all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d,e \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \in G
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \leq f
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi f
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \leq f
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo =
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∨
                        %mi e
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f = d \vee e
            %li
              %p
                Isotony: If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                is a distance function with
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \leq d
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi e
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
          %p
            It is possible to generate these even more systematically by specifying a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proarrow+equipment"} proarrow equipment
            and considering the (possibly symmetric)
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-object"} pro
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monads"} monads
            in it; see the
            %a{:href => "#proarrows"} Categorial interpretation
            below.
          %h3#unbiased_versions Unbiased versions
          %p
            Reflexivity and Transitivity are a binary–nullary pair whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unbiased"} unbiased
            combination is as follows:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#elementary"} Elementary
                version: For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0,1,2,\ldots
                and every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
                with
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≤
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi n
                      %mi e
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x_0,x_n) \leq \sum_{i \lt n} e(x_i,x_{i+})
              %p
                for each
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/list"} list
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi x
                          %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_0,\ldots,x_n \in X
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#sophisticated"} Sophisticated
                version: For every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0,1,2,\ldots
                and every
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in G
                such that
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ≤
                        %msup
                          %mi e
                          %mrow
                            %mo ∘
                            %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \leq e^{\circ n}
          %p
            We can combine these with Symmetry by generalizing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            from a natural number to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/list"} list
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϵ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bits"} bits
            and replacing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e(x_i,x_{i+})
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e(x_{i+},x_i)
            (that is, replacing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e^{\op}
            in the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \epsilon_i = 1
          %p
            Similarly, Nontriviality and Filtration are a binary–nullary pair whose unbiased version states (in light of Isotony) closure under finitary joins; but this is properly discussed at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
          %h3#structures_and_spaces Structures and spaces
          %p
            A collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            of distance functions that satisfies all of (1–6) is a
            = succeed ";" do
              %strong prometric
            = succeed "." do
              %strong quasi-prometric
            = succeed ";" do
              %strong symmetric
          %p
            Finally, a
            %strong prometric space
            is a set equipped with a prometric, and likewise a
            %strong quasi-prometric space
            is a set equipped with a quasi-prometric.
          %h3#generating_quasiprometrics Generating (quasi)-prometrics
          %p
            We sometimes wish to consider collections of distance functions that generate (quasi)-prometrics. In the following table, a collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            satisfying the conditions listed on the left has the name on the right:
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th Conditions
                %th Name
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1,2
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %strong pre-quasi-prometric
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1,2,3
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %strong pre-prometric
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}       4,5
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal+base"} ideal base
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1,2,  4,5
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  quasi-prometric
                  %strong
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base"} base
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1,2,3,4,5
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  prometric
                  %strong base
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}       4,5,6
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1,2,  4,5,6
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} quasi-prometric
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 1,2,3,4,5,6
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} prometric
          %p
            Here we always use the original (either
            %a{:href => "#elementary"} elementary
            or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#sophisticated"} sophisticated
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/centipede+mathematics"} centipede mathematics
            to actually give these things names.
          %p
            A (quasi)-prometric base is precisely an ideal base whose generated ideal is a (quasi)-prometric. We may also speak of a (quasi)-prometric
            %strong subbase
            as an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal+subbase"} ideal subbase
            (that is, an arbitrary collection) whose generated ideal base is a (quasi)-prometric base, or equivalently whose generated ideal is a (quasi)-prometric. A pre-(quasi)-prometric is always a (quasi)-prometric subbase, but not conversely; but thinking too hard about subbases risks more centipedes.
          %p
            A pre-quasi-prometric is
            %strong symmetric
            if its generated quasi-prometric is symmetric (hence a prometric); a quasi-prometric base is symmetric iff it is a prometric base (and the analogous result holds for subbases), but a symmetric pre-quasi-prometric need not be a pre-prometric. Some authors may require a strong version of Symmetry in which the distance functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            are all individually required to be
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+binary+function"} symmetric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) = d(y,x)
            (or simply
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = d^{\op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a prometric, then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} op
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{ d \in G \;|\; d = d^{\op} \}
          %p
            is a prometric base that generates
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            A pre-quasi-prometric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is
            %strong pointwise-bounded
            if every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \in G
            is pointwise-bounded; that is,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(x,y) \lt \infty
            for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in X
            (or simply
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d \lt \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a (quasi)-prometric, then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi b
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi d
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_b \coloneqq \{ d \in G \;|\; d \lt \infty \}
          %p
            is a (quasi)-prometric that is very similar to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (in particular, they are
            = succeed ")," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                uniformly equivalent
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/uniformly+equivalent"} ?
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_b
            %em not
            required, some authors may call the structure
            = succeed "," do
              %strong extended
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/red+herring+principle"} red herring principle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            is not pointwise-bounded. (It is possible that prometric spaces would work better with a closure condition that would make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_b
            generate
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Most definitions are no more complicated when phrased in terms of (quasi)-prometric bases or even pre-(quasi)-prometrics, and some constructions give one of these more naturally than the generated (quasi)-prometric. When working in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative mathematics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+class"} proper class
          %p
            Any (quasi)-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+space"} gauge
            is a (quasi)-prometric base; similarly, given any (quasi)-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudometric"} pseudometric
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+subset"} singleton
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{d\}
            is a (quasi)-prometric base (and its generated (quasi)-gauge in turn generates the same (quasi)-prometric). One might call a (quasi)-prometric (space)
            %em simple
            if it is generated in this way by a (quasi)-pseudometric; this term is used analogously in the theory of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntopogenous+spaces"} syntopogenous spaces
            %em (quasi)-pseudometrizable
            is more likely to be understood. (See
            %a{:href => "#subcategories"} Subcategories
            below.)
          %h2#morphisms Morphisms
          %p
            A
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+map"} short map
            between (quasi)-prometric spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to Y
            such that for every
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\in G_Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ×
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d\circ (f\times f) \in G_X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ProMet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ProMet
            for the category of prometric spaces and short maps, and similarly
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QProMet
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QProMet
            for the category of quasi-prometric spaces and short maps.
          %p
            If the (quasi)-prometrics of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are presented by bases, then this is equivalent to saying that for any basic distance function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d(f(x),f(x'))\le e(x,x')
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,x'\in X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gau
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gau
            of gauge spaces and short maps is included as a full subcategory of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ProMet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ProMet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QGau
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QGau
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QProMet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QProMet
          %h2#subcategories Subcategories
          %p
            Since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gau
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gau
            includes the categories of metric spaces and uniform spaces (disjointly), so does
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ProMet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ProMet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi QGau
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QGau
            includes the category of topological spaces (disjointly from metric and uniform spaces), so does
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi QProMet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} QProMet
          %p
            There is also another embedding of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif
            into
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ProMet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ProMet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Gau
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gau
            (both easier to state and not using
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+choice"} dependent choice
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"} uniform space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entourage"} entourage
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo ⊆
                  %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\subseteq X\times X
            a distance function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi U
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn ∞
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo ,
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ∉
                            %mi U
                            %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_U(x,y) =
                  \\begin{cases}
                  0 &amp; (x,y)\in U\\
                  \\infty &amp; (x,y)\notin U.
                  \\end{cases}
          %p
            (Again, this may be defined constructively as an infimum.) The collection of such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_U
            is a base for a prometric on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif
            into
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ProMet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ProMet
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,\infty\}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            by any positive real number also defines an embedding of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Unif
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif
            into
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ProMet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ProMet
          %p Conversely, every prometric induces a uniformity, where the entourages are the sets
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ϵ
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi ϵ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_{d,\epsilon} = \{ (x,y) \;|\; d(x,y) \lt \epsilon \} .
          %p
            In this way every short map induces a uniformly continuous map as well. This operation is compatible with the above inclusions of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Unif
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Unif
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Gau
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Gau
          %h2#proarrows Categorical interpretation
          %p
            As observed by Lawvere, an extended quasi-pseudo-metric space is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+enriched"} category enriched
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ≥
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([0,\infty],\geq,+,0)
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategory"} bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mi Mat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty] Mat
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrices"} matrices
            with values in this monoidal category. Analogously, an extended quasi-prometric space is a monad in the bicategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Pro
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mi Mat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pro [0,\infty] Mat
            whose hom-categories are the categories of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-object"} pro-object
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi Mat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,\infty] Mat
          %p
            Note that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rel
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mi Mat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel = \{0,1\} Mat
            denotes the bicategory of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation"} relation
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Rel
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rel
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Pro
                  %mi Rel
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Pro Rel
            is a quasi-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/uniform+space"}> uniform space
            \.
          %p
            In all these cases, in order to recover the correct notion of morphism abstractly, we must consider monads in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equipment"} equipment
            rather than merely a bicategory.
